# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
build/
dist/
develop-eggs/

# ── Machine-specific external-tool paths ────────────────
# Written by tools/configure_deps.py from what it finds on THIS machine, so it
# must never be committed: the paths are personal and the file would break
# everyone else's checkout by pinning it to one layout.
.env.local
activate_deps.bat
activate_deps.sh

# ── Virtual envs ────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── IDE / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Model weights (too large for git) ───────────────────
pretrained/
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.pkl
*.h5
*.hdf5

# The RL policy weights and the CG statistical potential are the exception: 275 KB
# and 9 KB, and `isrnaclong_pipeline` looks for them at `data/` on every run. They
# were on the development machine and not in the checkout, so Levels 2 and 3 ran
# with `policy_path=None` — a heuristic-only MCTS search — and nothing said so. The
# names are deliberately exact and not a `data/` wildcard: that way a file added to
# the directory later is still ignored by default.
!data/rl_policy_b0.pth
!data/rl_policy_bootstrap.pth
!data/cg_statistical_potential.pkl

# ── Bundled data (ships in the folder, never in git) ─────
# The deposited-structure database and the cgRNASP reference data travel with the working folder
# so that a copied directory is self-contained, and are listed here so that no future `git add -A`
# can stage them. This is the rule that exists because 4.9 GB once reached history and took three
# rounds of git filter-repo to remove.
_cgdata/

# ── External predictors (installed separately) ──────────
RNAbpFlow/
external/
rhofold/     # RhoFold+ checkout
msa_work/

# ── Run outputs (generated, large) ──────────────────────
output_*/
benchmark_*/
CIF_PDB_PSM/
_final_*.pdb
_final_out/
*.log

# ── Analysis intermediates ──────────────────────────────
# results/ reached 502 MB of .npz ensembles from an IBI sweep. They are
# regenerable from the scripts, and a repository that has absorbed them cannot
# easily give them back: the blobs stay in history. The reference tables the
# code actually loads are the ones under src/ and the committed checkpoints, not
# these.
results/
# Stray capture files from running the server by hand.
*_out.txt
*_err.txt

# ── Local config / private sequence ─────────────────────
# ROOT ONLY, and the leading slash is load-bearing. An unanchored `sequence.txt`
# also matches artifacts/2013nt/sequence.txt, which is committed on purpose: it is
# the demo target for run_2013nt.py, recovered from the shipped structure (see
# artifacts/README.md). Without the slash, `git add -A` silently omits the one file
# that makes the demo startable, and nothing says so.
/sequence.txt
test_*_ss.txt
# .claude/ is ignored except the iGEM AI-use notice
.claude/*
!.claude/RESPONSIBLE_AI_USE.md
# The project's Claude Code skills are source, not local configuration, and
# `CLAUDE.md` at the root already depends on this directory. Without this exception
# a skill written for the team stays on one machine: `.claude/skills/` is the path
# Claude Code loads project skills from, so the files have to travel with the
# checkout for anyone else to get them.
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
torusfold-paper/

# ── Runtime state written by the server, never source ───
# The feedback the form collects, beside the server that received it. It is one
# machine's inbox: committing it would publish whatever anyone typed, which is
# neither ours to publish nor useful to a reader of the repository.
feedback.json
# The web server's output directory: checkpoints, scratch PDBs, run logs.
output_web/
# Web-triggered runs from earlier invocations of the app.
output_2013nt/
results/plan_c/
# Local calibration sets downloaded for a scoring check.
_calib/
# The empty upload slot the PDB-upload endpoint writes into.
output_web/uploaded.pdb
